      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You’re right that, from a purely logical or cosmic standpoint, meaning isn’t handed to us—it’s not an objective fact. But the “math” changes if you include your own experience as a variable: the difference between staying and leaving isn’t zero *to you*, because you’re the one who feels the weight of that choice. Meaning isn’t discovered; it’s created, even if it’s temporary and fragile. And if both outcomes are truly equal, then you’re free to choose the one that leaves room for curiosity, connection, or even just a moment of relief—not because it’s “better,” but because it’s yours.",
